# UI Quality Gates

RULE: Every UI repo must pass these quality gates before merge. UI quality gates extend (not replace) the standard `scripts/quality-gates.sh` with UI-specific checks.

WHY: UI repos currently have inconsistent testing — some have vitest, some don't. Three repos in the March audit were flagged for missing vitest despite `testing_level=unit` in the manifest. Standardize now.

## Gate 1: Lint + Format (existing)

```bash
npx eslint src/ --max-warnings 0
npx prettier --check "src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}"
```

Already in quality-gates.sh for UI repos.

## Gate 2: TypeScript Strict (existing)

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit
```

All UI repos use strict TypeScript. No `any` types. No `@ts-ignore`.

## Gate 3: Component Tests (vitest)

```bash
CI=true npm test -- --run
```

**Minimum requirements:**
- Every shared component exported from ui-kit has at least one test
- Every page component has at least a render test (mounts without crash)
- DimensionalGrid, FilterBar, EntityLink, CrossLink need interaction tests (click, filter, sort)
- Use `vitest` with `pool: "forks"` (not threads — prevents zombie node processes)
- Use `@testing-library/react` for component testing

**What to test per component type:**

| Component Type | Must Test |
|---|---|
| Navigation (GlobalNavBar, SidebarNav, BreadcrumbNav) | Renders all links, highlights active, click navigates |
| Data display (DimensionalGrid, tables) | Renders data, sorts on click, filters reduce rows |
| Interactive (FilterBar, SelectionToolbar) | State changes on user interaction, URL params update |
| Cross-link (EntityLink, CrossLink) | Correct href generated, context params included |
| KPI cards (StatCard) | Renders value, label, delta; correct color for positive/negative |

## Gate 4: Build Smoke Test

```bash
VITE_MOCK_API=true npx vite build
```

Must build without errors. Tests that the app compiles with mock data.

## Gate 5: Accessibility (a11y)

**Automated checks (vitest-axe or similar):**
- Every interactive element has an accessible name
- Color contrast meets WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text)
- Focus is visible on all interactive elements (already using --color-border-focus)
- Tables have proper `<th>` headers
- Forms have associated labels

**Manual checks (Phase 7):**
- Keyboard navigation through all routes
- Screen reader announces page changes
- No keyboard traps

## Gate 6: Cross-Link Integrity

**Automated check (can be a vitest test or script):**
- Every `EntityLink` type maps to a valid surface in SurfaceRegistry
- Every `buildCrossLink()` target surface exists
- No hardcoded port numbers (grep for `localhost:51[0-9]{2}`)
- No hardcoded URLs to other UIs (must use SurfaceRegistry)

```bash
# Quick grep check for hardcoded ports
rg 'localhost:51[0-9]{2}' src/ --type ts --type tsx
# Should return 0 results (all ports come from SurfaceRegistry)
```

## Gate 7: No Orphan Deployments Route

```bash
# Every UI except deployment-ui should have zero /deployments routes
rg 'path.*deployments|to.*deployments' src/ --type ts --type tsx
# Should return 0 results in all non-Operations UIs
```

## Gate 8: Performance Budget

**Build size limits (vite build output):**
- Individual UI bundle: < 500KB gzipped (excluding shared chunks)
- Shared ui-kit chunk: < 150KB gzipped
- No single page component > 300 lines (split into sub-components)
- Images must be optimized (< 100KB each, prefer SVG)

**Runtime (manual, Phase 7):**
- First contentful paint: < 1.5s (mock mode)
- Time to interactive: < 2.5s (mock mode)
- DimensionalGrid with 1000 rows: renders in < 500ms (use virtualization)

## Quality Gate Script Template

For UI repos that don't have quality-gates.sh yet, use this template:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

echo "=== UI Quality Gates ==="

echo "[1/6] Lint..."
npx eslint src/ --max-warnings 0

echo "[2/6] Format..."
npx prettier --check "src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}"

echo "[3/6] TypeScript..."
npx tsc --noEmit

echo "[4/6] Tests..."
CI=true npm test -- --run 2>/dev/null || echo "WARN: No tests found"

echo "[5/6] Build..."
VITE_MOCK_API=true npx vite build

echo "[6/6] Cross-link check..."
if rg -q 'localhost:51[0-9]{2}' src/ --type ts 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "FAIL: Hardcoded port numbers found"
  exit 1
fi

echo "=== All gates passed ==="
```

## DO

- Run `CI=true npm test -- --run` before every commit to a UI repo
- Use `pool: "forks"` in vitest.config.ts
- Test cross-link URLs in component tests
- Keep page components under 300 lines

## NEVER

- Skip vitest in a UI repo (all must have tests)
- Use `pool: "threads"` (causes zombie node processes)
- Hardcode port numbers or URLs to other surfaces
- Ship a component without at least a render test

